{"overview":{"Symbol":"ANRO","Name":"Alto Neuroscience, Inc.","Description":"Alto Neuroscience, Inc. operates as a clinical-stage biopharmaceutical company in the United States. The company's product pipeline includes ALTO-100, which is in Phase 2b clinical trial for the treatment of patients with bipolar depression (BPD). It also develops ALTO-300, a small molecule melatonergic agonist and serotonergic antagonist with antidepressant properties, which is in Phase 2b clinical trial to treat patients with major depressive disorder (MDD); ALTO-101, a novel small molecule phosphodiesterase 4 inhibitor that is in Phase 2 proof-of-concept (POC) trial for the treatment of cognitive impairment associated with schizophrenia; ALTO-203, a novel small-molecule histamine H3 receptor inverse agonist, which is in Phase 2 POC trial to treat patients with MDD and higher levels of anhedonia; ALTO-202, an investigational orally bioavailable antagonist of the GluN2B subunit of the NMDA receptor that is in Phase 1 clinical trial for the treatment of MDD; and ALTO-208, a fixed-dose combination of pramipexole and aprepitant, an antiemetic, neurokinin-1 (NK-1) receptor antagonist for patients with Parkinson's disease for patients with Parkinson's disease. The company was incorporated in 2019 and is headquartered in Mountain View, California.","CIK":"","Exchange":"NYSE","Currency":"USD","Country":"United States","Sector":"Healthcare","Industry":"Biotechnology","Address":"650 Castro Street, Mountain View, CA, 94041, United States","FiscalYearEnd":"","LatestQuarter":"","MarketCapitalization":"726093632","EBITDA":"-77152000","PERatio":"","PEGRatio":"","BookValue":"6.943","DividendPerShare":"","DividendYield":"","EPS":"-2.43","RevenuePerShareTTM":"","ProfitMargin":"0","OperatingMarginTTM":"0","ReturnOnAssetsTTM":"-0.21706","ReturnOnEquityTTM":"-0.38856","RevenueTTM":"","GrossProfitTTM":"","DilutedEPSTTM":"-2.43","QuarterlyEarningsGrowthYOY":"","QuarterlyRevenueGrowthYOY":"","AnalystTargetPrice"